WEBVTT

00:00.200 --> 00:03.900
Moving from Dropbox to Google Drive?

00:04.200 --> 00:07.500
The usual ways send your files through someone else’s servers,

00:07.700 --> 00:11.100
or fill up your computer first.

00:11.300 --> 00:14.800
Stop halfway, and you’re left hunting for what’s missing.

00:15.600 --> 00:19.500
NexMove takes the straight line.

00:21.300 --> 00:23.900
Sign in to Dropbox.

00:24.400 --> 00:26.600
Sign in to Google.

00:27.100 --> 00:28.800
Press Start copying.

00:29.000 --> 00:32.900
Your files go from Dropbox, through your own PC, into Google Drive.

00:33.600 --> 00:37.600
No servers in between — not ours, not anyone’s.

00:38.200 --> 00:42.200
Nothing is saved to your hard drive.

00:42.600 --> 00:46.900
And if it stops, press Start again. It copies only what’s left.

00:47.300 --> 00:54.700
When it’s done, every file is checked against the original — so you can cancel Dropbox with confidence.

00:55.400 --> 01:00.000
NexMove, by K-NEX. Pay once. Coming soon for Windows.
